   "message": "KAFKA-20488 Write the ZK controller epoch to partition state znodes during migration\n\nZkTopicMigrationClient wrote state.kraftControllerEpoch() as the\ncontroller epoch of the partition state znodes in createTopic,\ncreateTopicPartitions and updateTopicPartitions. The ZK controller\ncompares that field with its own controller epoch, so it should be the\nZK controller epoch, which is what the request-level epoch in the RPCs\nsent by KRaftMigrationDriver already uses.\n\nThis patch passes state.zkControllerEpoch() instead and adds a\nregression test that makes the two epochs differ and reads the epoch\nback from the znode after each of the three methods.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
